  "sections": {
    "review": {
      "summary": "Owner answers in chat 2026-11-22: (1) ADR-007 approved with caveats: retroactively fetched data that was available at the time still applies; preserve reliable timestamps; define when data applies and how it refreshes rather than barring it. (2) Q-014 approved for integration only if it truly helps, after understanding how lines are set and measuring accuracy. (3) Agreed Lineup sit/start first; projections must explain why (player performance, position vs opposing defense, weather, injuries, depth charts, league scoring). Found ADR-007 called proposed in 9 places (ADR index, START_HERE, charter, REPO_MAP, GOVAI-013, model-integrity rule, arbit-model AGENTS, governance brief text, status), Q-012's 'Nothing fetches from NFL's API' superseded by OWN-040/041 (R-067), and R-063 treating weather as never a pre-game input.",
